      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The way vehicles in worlds work is down to the world/asset creator; there's no built-in \"flight engine\" in VRChat. It probably wouldn't be too difficult to modify a community-created prefab to have the properties you're asking for though, and more advanced features will likely become possible when Udon is implemented.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-02-24T08:01:28.328Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The currently used flight engine causes motion sickness by rotating the user with the vehicle, so people experience a rotation in VR that they don't experience in real life. \n\nBut people with roomscale tracking can fully rotate the head themselves to follow the verhicle rotation cause by the flight direction that is controlled by the controller. So the head rotation can be completely seperated from the flight vehicel rotation and only the position is translated to the head, causing no motion sickness. I tested this in my own game with multiple users and this solution came up as the best approach. It can be simply implemented like this:\n\ntransform.position = transform.position + (GameObject.FindGameObjectWithTag(RightController).transform.forward.normalized * (currentSpeed * Time.deltaTime));\n\nNote that \"transform.position\" is the position of the VR playspace / CameraRig",
